 web app  to visualize the robot and what we want  to add is an iOS app so I've taken the  robot to a couple of events so far and I  thought it would be cool sometimes I'm  walking between different demo booths  and walking between venues and I want to  check up on the BOTS make sure they're  all up and running like they should be  so I thought it'd be cool to build an  iOS app that does something similar to  what the web app does this is what the  app is going to look like it's going to  be a basic master detailed view  application so we've got a UI tableview  that's showing the  of all of the active box and then when  you click on one of the IDs it'll show  the detailed view of what that bot is  looking at so there's a picture I took  at my desk a couple days ago you can see  it recognize my face  and that I was smiling so it drew green  box around my face and I was holding up  a bottle of water the vision API was  able to identify that as a bottle of  water so what is the data going to look  like in firebase so at the root of our  firebase we have a splash box node and  then under that we have all the IDs for  our box and whenever one is updated we  want to change the color of that cell  and display how long ago the bot was  last active so here if it was active in  the last 60 seconds I'm displaying an  active now that's what the table view  looks like and this is a simplified  version of what the table view  controller code will look like so the  first thing we're doing is creating a  reference to our firebase and then we're  going to create a local bot array of F  data snapshot updated snapshot is the  data type of the snapshot that is  returned from firebase and then what we  want to do is we want to sync that data  from firebase into a local array so this  is pretty similar to what I did before  but we're listening on the value event  type and then we're going to loop  through all the bot I DS so we're going  to say for bot in snapshot children and  then with