f the rows in our table  view we want to prepare our segue so  we're going to set the bot I D -  whatever bot ID was selected and then  we're going to perform the segue bot  list - detail view and right here is  where we do that segue so in our  destination view controller which is  going to be the bot detail view  controller we're setting the name on  that view controller to the bots ID of  the bot that was selected and then  here's just the the functions we use to  set up our table view with our bot array  data so once we perform this segue we're  here in our bot detail view controller  which is pretty short so in here we're  just setting the title which is just the  heading on that view to the bots name  and then we're creating a new firebase  reference so this reference is going to  be slash BOTS slash whatever bot ID  we're viewing deb rel 5 in this example  and then we're adding another firebase  listener to listen to the data only for  that specific bot  so bot detail ref observe event type  we're listening on the value type again  here because we're not adding new data  to this node we're just resetting the  data every time a new image is taken by  the bot so we're grabbing all the data  returned from the vision API we can  think of this as the bots world so we  store that with the key of world and  then we basic see for decode the image  since we're storing the base64 image  string and firebase and then we get the  labels that are returned from the vision  aap  I and we loop through them and we  display them so the description is going  to be whatever the label was and then  score is going to be the confidence  score from the vision API and we're  going to display that as a percent we  add that to the label string and then we  just add some styling to the UI label so  again I just wanted to show you you know  an example of an app built with firebase  that's a little more complex than just  real-time chat and we can see that this  is super easy to do I've got a table  view controller and my detailed view  controller and all the data is  displaying in real time with firebase so  if we could go back to the slides  so just to recap as what we cover we  started with an overview of firebase  then I talked about how to get started  with firebase on iOS and we did one demo  of real time chat showed you how to  update a UI tableview with chat messages  stored in firebase and then we did a  second demo with the help from Cathy  Thank You Cathy  to show a bot visualizer app that I  built to visualize all the active cloud  vision bots and what they're looking at  at that point in time so if you want to  learn more the firebase documentation is  a great place to go  they've got awesome Doc's for every  platform iOS Android and web with  detailed guides on how to do all sorts  of things with firebase and then if you  want to learn more about the vision API  if you go to the Google cloud platform  github the cloud vision repo has a bunch  of getting started samples in all sorts  of platforms to get started with the  vision API there is an iOS sample in  Swift and objective-c and I encourage  you to get in touch with Google cloud  you can follow us on Twitter we have a  slack channel and we've got a bunch of  samples for all sorts of cloud products  on the Google cloud platform github and  thank you all for coming that's all I  got  you  you
 

